WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
A gambler offers a bet.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.530
He'll roll a fair dice four times.

3
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:07.440
You win if any roll shows a six.

4
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.510
The tempting maths: each
roll has a one in six chance,

5
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.280
so four rolls give four sixths.

6
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.190
About sixty-seven per cent.

7
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.360
Easy money?

8
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.060
But by that logic, six
rolls would give six sixths:

9
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.730
a guaranteed six.

10
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.140
Can that be right?

11
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.020
So is this bet really in your favour?

12
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll see that
separate rolls are independent:

13
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.280
one roll doesn't change the next.

14
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:38.110
You'll multiply probabilities when two
independent events must both happen.

15
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.820
And you'll discover that 'at least
one' is the opposite of 'none'.

16
00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: decide whether
this bet is better than evens.
